  "worked_solution": "The difference $B\u2216A$ consists of all the elements that are in $B$ but not $A.$ To represent $B\u2216A,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $B$ but not $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/7ec40584f82d7bd01aa7323ffb9cc4a53d631b74ea1d312d1b4141eb5da8d0d9.png)\n\nThe elements $a$ and $k$ are in $B$ but not $A.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nB\u2216A={a,k}.\n$$",
